    <description
  >How-To Videos: a qualified request counts as a vote for its requester (ADR 0003). When a Video Request&apos;s content or email changes, releases the vote it held for its old content and address (it stays if another request from that address still points there; a board vote that the request took over goes back to the board), then casts a vote keyed on the new content and the email in lower case, if that content is open for votes. If the person already voted on the board, that vote becomes the request&apos;s, so it cannot be withdrawn while the request stands. Two requests from one address saved together count once: the unique key refuses the second. Declined, Published and Retired content get no new vote. Runs in system context: team members hold no access to votes.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>Email_lowercase</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>LOWER({!$Record.SuppliedEmail})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>New_key</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression
    >{!$Record.HowTo_Content__c} &amp; LOWER({!$Record.SuppliedEmail})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Old_key</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression
    >{!$Record__Prior.HowTo_Content__c} &amp; LOWER({!$Record__Prior.SuppliedEmail})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel
  >How-To request vote {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>How-To: Request Counts as a Vote</label>
